{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 103, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty node2->output edge with a 3x3 conv creates a new learnable path, a much bigger gain than swapping out an existing op (exp 4)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on the missing direct input->output edge adds a whole new path, unlike replacing an existing skip (exp 13 vs exp 1)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the node1->output edge, the direct edge is one of very few paths to the output, so removing it is especially damaging (exp 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, removing edge 0 cuts node 2 off from the input too, collapsing the cell to at most the direct edge (exp 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 outputs zeros, so a conv on node1->node2 cannot add the benefit it normally does."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 1 is dead because edge 0 is none, upgrading the node1->output edge has no effect on accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing parameter-free pooling on the final edge with a 3x3 conv gains more than replacing a 1x1 conv (exp 6)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the input->node2 edge was missing creates a new deep path, so the gain exceeds an op swap."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual connection where none existed greatly improves trainability, while swapping a conv for skip on that edge is roughly neutral."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With no direct input->output edge, removing node2->output removes a large share of the remaining paths to the output (exp 16)."}], "tok": 7792, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "av